      "dcDescription": [
        "Guyana Amazon British Guiana Clay pot. The object is made of yellow-gray clay, which contained abundant particles of mica. Most likely, however, the glimpse is added. The pot has been built up by clay rolls. The shape is conical with the tip facing the bottom. The mouth is narrow with slightly turned edge. The vessel was used to store cassava beer in. It was owned by a woman in Sand Creek who received it in turn from the south of Wapishana. Diameter 62 cm Height 42 cm Dimensions diameter 23 cm. Wapishana 1962.28.0023 Guyana Amazonas Brittiska Guyana Lerkruka. Föremålet är gjort av gulgrå lera,"
      ],
